  "question": {
    "text": "If the line $y=m x+1$ meets the circle $x^2+y^2+3 x=0$ in two points equidistant from and on opposite sides of $x$-axis, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SxS6J",
      "text": "\n$3 m+2=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6mtfI",
      "text": "\n$3 m-2=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "m24ky",
      "text": "\n$2 m+3=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e5dqP",
      "text": "\n$2 m-3=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Circle: $x^2+y^2+3 x=0$\nCentre, $B=\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}, 0\\right)$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/JHi0ISQLksCBFrolS3C21H_y9kJM4wr3_4-6d-o3ePs.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$y$-intercept of the line $=1$\n$$\n\\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{A}=(0,1)\n$$\nSlope of line, $m=\\tan \\theta=\\frac{O A}{O B}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow m=\\frac{1}{\\frac{3}{2}}=\\frac{2}{3} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 3 m-2=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
